---
title: "input_decoding (EIP-7951: Precompile for secp256r1 Curve Support)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_read_h: h = input[0..32] (BigEndian)
    q_read_h --> q_read_r: r = input[32..64] (BigEndian)
    q_read_r --> q_read_s: s = input[64..96] (BigEndian)
    q_read_s --> q_read_qx: qx = input[96..128] (BigEndian)
    q_read_qx --> q_read_qy: qy = input[128..160] (BigEndian)
    q_read_qy --> [*]: return (h, r, s, qx, qy)
    note right of q_read_qy
        INV-001: Input is exactly 160 bytes, split into five 32-byte fields
        INV-002: All fields are BigEndian-encoded unsigned integers
        INV-003: Scalars (h, r, s) are not required to be less than n at decoding stage
    end note
